# Cloudflare Pages redirects — 3locksmiths.co.il
#
# ⚠️ THE RULES BELOW ARE A FALLBACK. The 301 that production actually serves for these paths comes
# from a ZONE-LEVEL Cloudflare Redirect Rule, not from this file. Read both sections before editing.
#
# ── THE PAGES DEFECT THIS FILE CANNOT ESCAPE ───────────────────────────────────
#
# Deployed and measured 2026-09-02 against production, before the zone rule existed:
#
#   UPPERCASE request  /locations/%D7%A9%D7%9B...%9C/   -> 301 -> /%D7%90%D7%96...%AA/   ✅ rule fires
#   lowercase request  /locations/%d7%a9%d7%9b...%9c/   -> 404                            ❌ no match
#
# Cloudflare Pages UPPERCASE-NORMALISES the source path of a rule at parse time, then matches it
# against the RAW request path. This site emits LOWERCASE %d7% everywhere — sitemap.xml, every
# canonical, every authored href — so every real URL is lowercase and can never match a rule in
# this file. Writing the rule in lowercase does not help: it is normalised to uppercase too. Raw
# unencoded Hebrew does not help: dalita.co.il proves it normalises to uppercase as well.
#
# THE ASYMMETRY THAT HIDES THIS: static ASSET lookup IS case-insensitive — both cases of a live
# page return 200 — while RULE matching is case-sensitive. So poking a live URL by hand tells you
# nothing about whether a rule would match, and a reviewer who tests only assets concludes the
# opposite of the truth. I made exactly that error on the first pass.
#
# ── THE FIX, DEPLOYED AND VERIFIED 2026-09-02 ──────────────────────────────────
#
# Cloudflare → 3locksmiths.co.il → Rules → Overview → Redirect Rules, named
# "Withdrawn cities → service areas hub":
#
#   If:   lower(http.request.uri.path) in { the seven paths listed below }
#   Then: Static redirect -> https://3locksmiths.co.il/%d7%90%d7%96%d7%95%d7%a8%d7%99-%d7%a9%d7%99%d7%a8%d7%95%d7%aa/  301
#
# `lower()` is the entire point: it matches BOTH encodings, which nothing in this file can do.
# Verified on deployment — all seven cities return 301 in lowercase AND uppercase, one hop,
# landing 200 on the hub, and all 25 surviving location pages still return 200 (no over-match).
#
# IT ALSO OUTRANKS THE CACHE. Cloudflare held stale 200s of the withdrawn pages under a 7-day
# s-maxage that NEITHER a fresh deploy NOR a zone "Purge Everything" cleared — both were tried on
# 2026-09-02: `Age` kept climbing and cf-cache-status stayed DYNAMIC, while 3locksmiths.pages.dev
# itself already returned 404. The stale copy lives in the Pages asset layer, which a zone purge
# does not reach. Redirect Rules execute BEFORE cache lookup, so the stale copy is never consulted.
# That is why the rule fixed the symptom instantly instead of waiting out the TTL.
#
# WHY KEEP THIS FILE: it is version-controlled and travels with the repo, so it still catches
# uppercase traffic if the zone rule is ever deleted. Defence in depth, not the mechanism.
#
# ⚠️ FLEET-WIDE: every sibling site with Hebrew slugs has the same latent defect. galbath.co.il's
# uppercase rules only catch uppercase traffic; dalita.co.il's raw-Hebrew rules likewise. None of
# them redirect the lowercase URLs their own sitemaps publish, and none has a zone rule yet.
#
# Ships in out/ from public/ (next build copies public/ wholesale). wrangler auto-detects it —
# ops/deploy-site.ps1 does not special-case it; line 255 is a plain `npx wrangler pages deploy`.
# Format: <from>  <to>  <status>. First match wins.
#
# NO WILDCARDS UNDER /locations/. _redirects outranks existing static assets on Pages, and a
# `/locations/*` catch-all cannot be fenced off — the per-survivor rules that would protect the
# 25 live city pages get uppercase-normalised too, so lowercase survivor traffic would fall
# through the fence and be redirected away. Exact paths only.
#
# ── WHY THESE SEVEN ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Seven location pages withdrawn 2026-09-02 because the business no longer services those cities
# (docs/business-facts.md §E.1). באר שבע and ירושלים are original pre-migration WordPress
# permalinks, which is why CLAUDE.md golden rule 5 requires a redirect plan rather than a bare
# deletion; the other five were generated by this project and are redirected too because they
# were live and in the sitemap.
#
# ⚠️ THEY HELD NO RANKING SIGNAL. Search Console URL Inspection on all seven, 2026-09-02:
# "URL is unknown to Google — last crawled: never". An earlier version of this comment asserted
# they "return 404 on the form Google indexed" — that was never measured, and it is false. The
# redirect earns its place for people following old links and for honesty about coverage, not to
# rescue rankings. Do not let that false premise justify urgency it does not deserve.
#
# Target is the service-areas hub, not the homepage: a visitor who searched for a specific city
# can self-select one that is actually served, and the hub no longer claims the withdrawn ones.
# Not a nearest-city map — there is no honest substitute for ירושלים or באר שבע among the
# survivors, and Google treats a redirect to a non-equivalent page as a soft 404 anyway.
#
# ── VERIFYING ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
